# /sdd-scan

Purpose:
  Run security pattern scans against code files using the sdd-adapter
  hook-bridge runtime. Surfaces CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW findings
  with severity, line numbers, and remediation guidance.

Owns: commands/sdd-scan.sdd

Description:
  Bridges .sdd/security/ controls with the sdd-adapter runtime to
  scan files against base patterns and language-specific skill patterns.
  Base RuntimePatternSet always runs; SkillPatternSets activate when
  file_path extension matches a registered programming language skill.
  Supports fail-open on spec load failure and fail-closed on CRITICAL/HIGH.

Usage:
  /sdd-scan
  /sdd-scan --file <path>
  /sdd-scan --directory <path>
  /sdd-scan --severity <level>
  /sdd-scan --language <language>
  /sdd-scan --json

Options:
  --file        Scan a single file
  --directory   Scan all files in directory recursively
  --severity    Filter by severity (CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW)
  --language    Filter by language skill (go, python, etc.)
  --json        Output machine-readable JSON

Mode: READ_ONLY

SecurityLevels:
  L0: informational
  L1: low
  L2: medium
  L3: high
  L4: critical
  L5: block

ScanBehavior:
  base_patterns: always run against all content
  skill_patterns: activate only when file extension matches registered language skill
  fail_open: on spec load failure, return PASS with warning
  fail_closed: on CRITICAL or HIGH findings, exit code 2

Output:
  SECURITY SCAN

    Files Scanned:    <count>
    Findings:         <count>
      CRITICAL:       <count>
      HIGH:           <count>
      MEDIUM:         <count>
      LOW:            <count>
    Decision:         PASS | WARN | BLOCK

  Findings Detail:
    [CRITICAL] pattern: hardcoded-secret | file: src/payment.go:42
      message: Hardcoded API key detected
      remediation: Move secret to environment variable or vault

    [HIGH] pattern: sql-injection | file: src/api.go:108
      message: String concatenation in SQL query
      remediation: Use parameterized queries

Rules:
  [SCN-01] /sdd-scan MUST NOT modify any scanned files.
  [SCN-02] Scan results MUST include pattern ID, severity, line number, and message.
  [SCN-03] CRITICAL and HIGH findings MUST trigger BLOCK decision.
  [SCN-04] Spec load failures MUST result in PASS with warning, not error.
  [SCN-05] Skill patterns MUST only activate for matching file extensions.
  [SCN-06] Scan results MUST be persisted to .sdd/runtime/scan-results/ for audit.

